From 853a8da7552831af4123d212efa7b8c76ecfdf0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Lamm <hanklammiv@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:16:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Optional top-K candidate dump (--topk K --tol T)

fit_theta_all_best_one_theta.py: new flags --topk (default 0 = unchanged
behaviour), --tol, --topk_vec_slack, --topk_txt, --topk_format
{matrix,vector}, --topk_append.  Pass 2 enumerates all root combinations
within (tol*slack)*best vector distance, ranks them by the true matrix
Frobenius distance to R_z(theta), dedups identical exact matrices, keeps
frob <= tol*best (at most K) and writes them in the fits_f=N.txt format
plus ", frob , rank" (also <prefix>.theta_topk.npz).

dump_special_thetas.py: --topk K [--tol T --fs 4,6,...] post-processes the
existing out.phase_free_special_theta.npz: ranks every stored matrix against
each special theta and writes fits_topk_f=N.txt.  No flags = old behaviour.

tools.py: householder_int_matrix() exact integer 3^e*V (no Sage parsing).
run_topk: theta-list driver.

